  "connectionHelp": "1. Connect this device and the robot to the same network.\n\n2. Start rosbridge and rosapi on the robot.\n\n3. Enter the robot host and WebSocket port. The default port is 9090.\n\nFor TLS or a reverse-proxy path, enter a full ws:// or wss:// URL. A port included in the URL takes precedence.\n\nDirect ROS 2: no rosbridge needed. The phone joins the robot's ROS 2 network like another node. Use the same Wi-Fi as the robot and its ROS_DOMAIN_ID (usually 0). The robot IP is optional; enter it if the network blocks multicast. Messages from packages the app does not know cannot be shown.\n\nZenoh: for robots running ROS 2 with RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_zenoh_cpp. Enter the robot address (its Zenoh router, port 7447 unless you add another) and its ROS_DOMAIN_ID. One TCP connection, no multicast, so it also works across networks, over a VPN, or over USB with adb reverse.",
